# Vue 3.5+ (TypeScript)

Current Vue 3.5 APIs in `<script setup lang="ts">`. No Vue 2, Options API, mixins, or `this.`. Follow `typescript.mdc`.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { computed, useId, useTemplateRef, watch } from 'vue'

interface Props {
  title: string
  kicker?: string
}

const { title, kicker = '' } = defineProps<Props>()
const model = defineModel<string>()
const headingId = useId()
const formEl = useTemplateRef('contact-form')
const isReady = computed(() => title.length > 0)

watch(() => title, () => {
  /* getter required for destructured props */
})
</script>

<template>
  <section :aria-labelledby="headingId">
    <h2 :id="headingId">{{ title }}</h2>
  </section>
</template>
```

- Type-based macros only: `defineProps<T>()`, `defineEmits<{ change: [id: string] }>()`, `defineModel<T>()`.
- Prop defaults: native destructure (Vue 3.5 reactive props destructure). Do not use `withDefaults` unless a rare case forbids destructure.
- `useTemplateRef('name')` (not `ref(null)` string matching). `useId()` for labels; never inside `computed`.
- `ref<T>()` / `computed(() => …)` let inference work; add a generic when the initial value is not enough.
- Generic lists: `<script setup lang="ts" generic="T">` on the primitive, not a `any[]` prop.
- Boolean names: `is` / `has` / `can`. Named exports in `.ts`. PascalCase multi-word components (`HeroSection`). Directories kebab-case.
- Client-only APIs behind `onMounted` or `import.meta.env.SSR`.
- Local state. No Pinia unless two distant trees must share it. VueUse only when it replaces non-trivial code.

## Do not

```vue
<script>
export default { props: { title: String }, data() { return {} } }
</script>
```
